    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac\\pi2,\\dfrac{7\\pi}6,\\dfrac{11\\pi}6$.",
      "worked": "Let $P(u)=2u^3-11u^2+4u+5$. Since $P(1)=0$, $u-1$ is a factor.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(u)&=(u-1)(2u^2-9u-5)\\\\P(u)&=(u-1)(2u+1)(u-5).\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=\\sin x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin x-1)(2\\sin x+1)(\\sin x-5)&=0\\\\\\sin x&=1,-\\frac12,5.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $\\sin x=5$ because $-1\\le\\sin x\\le1$. For $0\\le x\\le2\\pi$,\n$$x=\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{7\\pi}6,\\frac{11\\pi}6.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
